course: dictionary
lesson: 10035
title: Terminate: to end or stop
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Terminate is a formal word that means to end something, or to come to an end. «The contract was terminated» means the contract was ended, so it no longer goes on. Look at the words around it: a contract is an agreement, and an agreement that is ended stops working.
explain: Context can also show you a different meaning. «This train terminates here, all change.» The clue is all change: passengers must get off, so the train stops here and goes no further. Terminate here means end here.
explain: Maths uses terminate too. A decimal that stops, like 0.25, is a terminating decimal, because it has a last digit. 1/3 = 0.333… does not terminate, because the threes go on for ever.
fact: Terminate means to end something, or to come to an end.
fact: «The contract was terminated» means the contract was brought to an end.
fact: Terminate is a formal word; end and stop are everyday words with the same meaning.
fact: A train or bus that terminates at a place stops there and goes no further.
fact: A terminating decimal stops, like 0.25; 1/3 = 0.333… does not terminate because it goes on for ever.
exercise: «This bus terminates at the station.» What does terminates mean here? | Breaks down on the road | Waits at the stop for a while | *Stops there and goes no further | Leaves the station and goes on to the next town
exercise: Which decimal is a terminating decimal? | *0.25 | 0.666… | 0.1666… | 0.333…
exercise: A letter says «Your membership is terminated.» What does it mean? | *Your membership has ended | Your membership is being printed | Your membership has grown bigger | Your membership is free for ever
test: What does it mean to terminate a call? | Make the call louder | *End the call | Start the call again | Record the call for later
test: Which word means the same as terminate? | *End | Repeat | Begin | Continue
exam: In maths, what is a terminating decimal? | A decimal with no zeros in it | A decimal that is always bigger than one | *A decimal that stops, with a last digit, like 0.25 | A decimal that goes on for ever
